; ── mlx_shim — the VENDORED mlx parser's compiler-libs shim (lib 1 of 3) ─────────────────────────
; Vendored verbatim from mlx 0.11 (mlx/mlx_shim.ml). It re-exports the handful of compiler-libs
; values the OCaml-grammar files reach for under the Astlib-shadowed AST (Location.error, mkloc,
; Longident.last, Pprintast.tyvar), bridging ppxlib's Astlib view to Ocaml_common.
;
; Kept as its OWN unwrapped library: a single wrapped library hits the compiler's "Warnings is
; dangling" shadow snag, and folding the shim into the wrapped parser library hits a menhir
; "Parser depends on the wrapper" cycle. The shim-as-leaf + rt + parser split (see ../rt, ../parser)
; sidesteps both. -w -a silences the upstream OCaml-stdlib warnings we do not own.
(library
 (name mlx_shim)
 (flags
  (:standard -w -a -open Astlib -open Astlib.Ast_501))
 (libraries ppxlib ocaml-compiler-libs.shadow))
